{
  "$comment": [
    "Tool Policy (proposed C41) seed rows: one row per MCP tool, from document 24, sections 2.2, 2.3 and 6.1, and tools.json. C41 is still a proposal (document 20, section 2.10). The config schema validates this file as a preset entity file. It joins a preset only when C41 is adopted.",
    "allowedRoleKeys: the roles of tools.json defaultRoles.roleKeys. Where the default is a relation, the roles come from the document 24, section 2.2 table: any role and anyone signed in give all 14 human roles; an owner relation gives application-owner; a record relation gives the roles with W in that toolset. The engine still checks the relation, as each row's description says. C41 has no column for a relation, so requiresOwnerRole stays false: no tool needs every caller to own the application.",
    "maxAiState: the furthest AI write state of the tool in tools.json. Configuration can only tighten it. The engine contract caps it whatever this row says.",
    "callsPerPersonPerHour is left out: document 24 gives no default. A missing value means no per-person limit until an adopter sets one.",
    "WORKING DEFAULT (open design question 9). aiMaySubmit is yes for intake requests, change requests, decisions and configuration drafts on submit_record, and for review requests on request_architecture_review.",
    "WORKING DEFAULT (open design question 8). submit_record: the engine accepts without a card only for the locked list.",
    "WORKING DEFAULT (open design question 4). propose_configuration_change: a person accepts the exact diff on one card.",
    "WORKING DEFAULT (open design question 7). record_deployment: AI-only code approvals never count as authorization.",
    "WORKING DEFAULT (open design question 12). No row names a workload role. deployment-recorder and approval-writer call no MCP tool; pipelines use the record endpoint under a Workload Grant (C42).",
    "Rows change like any configuration row: through a configuration draft and an accepted decision. No tool writes them."
  ],
